                      (        forth.asm):00296         * Writable dictionary section begins right here. We cannot have anything
                      (        forth.asm):00297         * statically defined at this point. Therefore, FORTHIN moves the code for @
                      (        forth.asm):00298         * to this location and sets up DICEND and LSTWAD accordingly. All the RAM
                      (        forth.asm):00299         * beyond this point (after the reallocated @ implementation) is user defined
                      (        forth.asm):00300         * material. Note that builtin words, though they cannot be forgotten (to the
                      (        forth.asm):00301         * extent they are ROM resident--not to mention inter-word dependencies),
                      (        forth.asm):00302         * might still be overridden by user definitions. WORDS will happily ignore
                      (        forth.asm):00303         * that fact and list everything in the dictionary linked list order.
