                      (        forth.asm):00314         * Book" for a description of interrupt stacks in native 6309 mode.
E000 8EFF0A           (        forth.asm):00315 (3)     IODZHDL ldx     #DV0ERRM        Assume division by zero TRAP
E003 C6F6             (        forth.asm):00316 (2)             ldb     #EDIVZR         "Division by zero" error code
E005 113C80           (        forth.asm):00317 (4)             bitmd   #$80            Division by zero?
E008 2608             (        forth.asm):00318 (3)             bne     @reslvd
E00A 113C40           (        forth.asm):00319 (4)             bitmd   #$40            Illegal opcode...
E00D 8EFF04           (        forth.asm):00320 (3)             ldx     #IOPERRM        ...is the only other possibility
E010 C6EB             (        forth.asm):00321 (2)             ldb     #ENOSUP         "Operation not supported" error code
E012 E762             (        forth.asm):00322 (4+1)   @reslvd stb     2,s             Pass error code to SYSTHR8 (via B)
E014 BDE2E4           (        forth.asm):00323 (7)             jsr     PUTS
E017 EC6C             (        forth.asm):00324 (5+1)           ldd     12,s            Return code address (PC)
E019 108E01DF         (        forth.asm):00325 (4)             ldy     #HEXBUF
E01D BDE187           (        forth.asm):00326 (7)             jsr     HDMP4
E020 8E01DF           (        forth.asm):00327 (3)             ldx     #HEXBUF
E023 BDE2E4           (        forth.asm):00328 (7)             jsr     PUTS
E026 BDE2CA           (        forth.asm):00329 (7)             jsr     PUTSP
                      (        forth.asm):00330         
                      (        forth.asm):00331         * Observability: preserve the user return address in the system stack.
                      (        forth.asm):00332         * This is similar to what we do in FIRQ/@sigint, except that the interrupt
